   "id": "yevamot.40a.17",
   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "הַכּוֹנֵס אֶת יְבִמְתּוֹ וְכוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא — ״יָקוּם עַל שֵׁם אָחִיו״ אָמַר רַחֲמָנָא, וַהֲרֵי קָם.",
   "en": "The mishna states: «One who consummates» levirate marriage with his yevama thereby acquires his deceased brother’s property. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? «The Merciful One states» in the Torah: «“He shall succeed in the name of his» dead «brother”» (Deuteronomy 25:6), «and he has succeeded» him by marrying his wife; consequently, he succeeds him by acquiring his property as well."
  }
